# What `sm scan` skips in this repository (scripts/skill_map_scan.py).
# Same syntax as .gitignore. Committed on purpose: this file decides which
# files become nodes, which decides the finding counts, which decides the
# skill-map gate's verdict. Leaving it untracked would make the gate depend on
# whichever defaults `sm init` happened to write on that machine — the same
# reason PINNED_VERSION exists in the runner.
#
# `sm init` writes a default copy only when none exists and never overwrites
# this one, so re-running init is safe.

# --- Version control, dependencies, OS noise (upstream defaults) -------------
.git/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
*.log

# --- Build output (upstream defaults) ----------------------------------------
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
.cache/
.tmp/

# skill-map's own state, and the agent-process skill `sm agent install`
# materialises. This repository never runs that verb — the runner's allowlist
# rejects it — but the entry is kept so the default behaviour is not silently
# altered if someone does.
.skill-map/
sm-process-jobs/

# --- Generated by graphify ----------------------------------------------------
# The single most important entry here. CI runs `graphify update .` immediately
# before the harness scan, so this tree exists on a runner and usually does not
# on a laptop. Left scannable, its wiki Markdown enters the graph as ~14 extra
# nodes, and the node and link counts then differ between CI and every laptop.
#
# Excluding it makes nodes and links identical in both environments. The
# CLAUDE.md pointers into this tree are additionally covered by the committed
# ignored-references match-list on core/reference-broken
# (.skill-map/settings.json), so they are never reported broken on a laptop
# where the tree does not exist — the historical CI/laptop ±1 swing in the
# reference-broken count is gone.
graphify-out/

# --- Python and Rust build artefacts -----------------------------------------
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.venv*/
venv/
rust/toon/bin/

# --- dbt output and vendored packages -----------------------------------------
# `dbt build` writes target/ and installs third-party packages into
# dbt_packages/. Neither is harness content, and the vendored packages carry
# their own docs whose links are not ours to keep green — the same reasoning
# tests/test_docs_links.py uses to skip them.
target/
dbt_packages/
logs/

# --- Activation mirrors and pack-side component copies ------------------------
# `scripts/activate_skill_stack.sh` materialises the active pack twice:
#
#   1. `references/` and `templates/` at the repository ROOT are byte-for-byte
#      copies of the pack's own `skill-packs/<pack>/{references,templates}/`.
#      Scanning both double-counts every doc node and makes token totals lie.
#      The pack copy is the editing source ("edit the pack copy, never the
#      root mirror -- activation overwrites it", README), so the pack side
#      stays scanned and the root mirror is excluded. Links from live skills
#      (`../../references/<file>.md`) keep resolving: `reference-broken`
#      checks the graph *or the disk*, same as the graphify-out/ entry above.
#
#   2. `.claude/` is LAYERED from `skill-packs/*/.claude/` (shared pack first,
#      then domain pack). The live tree is where skill-map's provider detection
#      assigns real kinds (skill/command/agent) and where collisions and
#      reserved names are checked; the pack-side copies scan kind-blind as
#      plain markdown, double-counting all 38 skills and contributing phantom
#      `reference-broken` findings (their `../../references/` links only
#      resolve after activation flattens them to the root). Scan the live
#      tree, exclude the pack-side component copies. Pack-side references/
#      and templates/ are NOT matched by this pattern and remain scanned.
#
# Leading slashes anchor at the repository root on purpose: a bare
# `references/` would also swallow `skill-packs/<pack>/references/` -- the
# exact opposite of the intent.
/references/
/templates/
/skill-packs/*/.claude/
